# Seeds for `mise run parity-regression`, one per line.
#
# A seed goes in here when a parity run found something with it. The nightly run
# (.github/workflows/parity.yml) draws a fresh seed each time and so never
# repeats itself; these are replayed on every pull request, which is what keeps a
# divergence that was once found from coming back unnoticed. The same division as
# testdata/fuzz-corpus/ and the nightly fuzz run.
#
# Reproduce one with:
#
#     ./bin/itest --parity --parity-seed <seed> --parity-runs 400 -v
#
# The queries a seed produces depend on the generator, so editing
# src/itest/parity_gen.odin changes what these replay. That is expected and not a
# reason to avoid editing it: the seeds are a supply of awkward traffic, not a
# fixed set of cases, and the properties they are checked against live in
# parity_compare.odin where they can be read.

# An upstream that had issued a cookie was owed one on every reply after it -
# including replies to queries this server had sent without one, which is what a
# client asking without EDNS produces. The correct cookie-less reply was thrown
# away and the client waited out the upstream timeout. Fixed in
# src/upstream/cookie.odin; the named case is in src/itest/cases_cookie.odin.
1
